# Generated reports — regenerate with `just report` / `just validate-all`
reports/
# ...except the research manifest, which is NOT regenerable. It records what
# was actually paid for: which novel terms were researched, how long each took,
# and which failed and why. Re-running would cost the whole batch again.

# Generated from the LinkML schema by `just gen-schema`
src/naturalproductmech/schema/naturalproductmech_dataclasses.py

# Local overrides
.env
CLAUDE.local.md
local/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# The batch runner's console log stays ignored: it is the tail a human watches,
# and the manifest above is the durable record of the same run.

downloads/

# The site's embedding artifacts. The two MAPS are committed, because the site
# renders from them and a checkout without them would render a different site.
# The text vectors are not: large, and rebuildable from the corpus with
# `just embed`.
data/embeddings/*.npy
data/embeddings/ids.json
data/embeddings/records.json
data/embeddings/meta.json
downloads/

# The curation backlog is DERIVED — `just worklist` recomputes it from the
# corpus, and a row leaves a queue when the thing that put it there changes.
# `just review-queue --tsv` writes this checkpoint for one curation session;
# committing it would be committing a stale answer to a question that is
# always cheap to re-ask.
curation/record_review_queue.tsv
